@*
    A text field with a list of suggestions under it: the ARIA 1.2 editable
    combobox with list autocomplete. What is typed is free and filters nothing; the
    options are suggestions a reader can take instead of typing — the planned-hours
    presets are the first host. Built as TagMultiSelect is and for its reasons: no
    interop, a real listbox in the DOM, the focus in the input the whole time, and
    `aria-activedescendant` moving the reading cursor instead of the focus.

    The keys, per the APG pattern. Down, or Alt+Down, opens the list; Down and Up
    then move the active option and wrap. Enter on an active option takes it and
    closes the list; Enter with none active commits what was typed. Escape closes
    an open list, or clears the field when the list is already closed. Tab closes
    the list without taking anything. A click in the field opens the list too, so a
    pointer has the suggestions within reach. Which of those keys keep their browser
    default is decided in components.js by the input's class, for the reason the
    tag picker's note there gives: a decision the server makes arrives a key late.

    A key the open list used is not the host's as well. The input's
    `@onkeydown:stopPropagation` is bound to whether the list is drawn, so while it
    is, a Blazor `@onkeydown` above it — the Calendar hours editor's Escape-cancels —
    never hears the Escape that closed the list or the Enter that took an option.
    Bound to the state drawn *before* the key, which is the state the key acted on,
    so this is not the one-key-late flag components.js describes: that one is set by
    the key it means to stop. Blazor's flag ends only Blazor's own walk; a document
    listener in script still hears the key.

    A value is committed three ways, each reported once through OnCommit with its
    reason: a pick, Enter, or a native `change` — the field left, or Enter in a
    browser that raises one. A change carrying the value just committed is not
    reported again, which is what keeps Enter from committing twice: the browser
    follows the keydown with a change for the same text. A host that will not keep
    the value calls Refuse on it, and the field goes back to the last value that
    stood: the last one committed and kept, or the last figure the host set.

    The field's text is the host's Value only until somebody types, as in TextField:
    the host's figure is taken when the host changes it, so a re-render that hands
    the same Value back does not wipe what is being typed. A host bound two-way
    echoes each keystroke back as Value; an echo is the text already in the field,
    so it is not taken as a new figure — it moves neither the last committed text
    (the field left after typing still reports Changed) nor what Refuse goes back to.
*@

<div class="@ClassValue" data-testid="@TestId">
    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Label))
    {
        <label class="field__label" for="@InputId">@Label</label>
    }

    <input id="@InputId"
           class="@InputClass"
           type="text"
           role="combobox"
           autocomplete="off"
           @bind:get="_text"
           @bind:set="SetTextAsync"
           @bind:event="oninput"
           placeholder="@Placeholder"
           disabled="@Disabled"
           aria-expanded="@(ListShown ? "true" : "false")"
           aria-controls="@ListId"
           aria-autocomplete="list"
           aria-activedescendant="@ActiveOptionId"
           aria-label="@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Label) ? AriaLabel : null)"
           @onclick="OpenOnCurrent"
           @onblur="Close"
           @onchange="OnChangeAsync"
           @onkeydown="OnKeyDownAsync"
           @onkeydown:stopPropagation="ListShown"
           @attributes="AdditionalAttributes" />

    @if (ListShown)
    {
        @* preventDefault on mousedown keeps the focus in the input, so the blur that
           closes the list cannot land before the click that takes an option. *@
        <ul id="@ListId" class="combobox__list" role="listbox" aria-label="@ListLabel" data-testid="@Part("list")">
            @for (var i = 0; i < Options.Count; i++)
            {
                var index = i;
                var option = Options[index];
                <li id="@OptionId(index)"
                    class="@OptionClass(index)"
                    role="option"
                    aria-selected="@(index == _activeIndex ? "true" : "false")"
                    data-value="@option.Value"
                    data-testid="@Part($"option-{index}")"
                    @onmousedown:preventDefault="true"
                    @onclick="() => PickAsync(option)">@option.Label</li>
            }
        </ul>
    }
</div>

@code {
    private readonly string _id = "combobox-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
    private string _text = string.Empty;
    private string? _hostValue;
    private string _committed = string.Empty;
    private string _standing = string.Empty;
    private bool _open;
    private int _activeIndex = -1;

    /// <summary>The suggestions, in the order the list draws them. Taking one puts its
    /// <see cref="SelectorOption.Value"/> in the field; the list reads its label.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<SelectorOption> Options { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The host's value. Taken into the field whenever it changes.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Value { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Every edit: each keystroke, a pick, and Escape clearing the field.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> ValueChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A value was committed — picked, entered or changed. See
    /// <see cref="ComboboxCommit"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<ComboboxCommit> OnCommit { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? Label { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The field's accessible name where there is no visible label.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? AriaLabel { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The list's accessible name. Defaults to the field's.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? ListAriaLabel { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? Placeholder { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public bool Disabled { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The small inline field, as <see cref="TextField.Compact"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Compact { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The input's id, for a host that sends the focus to it.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Id { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Appended to <c>combobox</c> on the wrapper.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Lands on the wrapper; the list and each option take it as a prefix.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Splatted onto the input — <c>inputmode</c>, for one.</summary>
    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? AdditionalAttributes { get; set; }

    private bool ListShown => _open && Options.Count > 0 && !Disabled;

    private string InputId => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Id) ? _id : Id;

    private string ListId => InputId + "-list";

    private string OptionId(int index) => $"{InputId}-option-{index}";

    private string? ActiveOptionId => ListShown && _activeIndex >= 0 && _activeIndex < Options.Count
        ? OptionId(_activeIndex)
        : null;

    private string? ListLabel => ListAriaLabel ?? Label ?? AriaLabel;

    private string ClassValue
    {
        get
        {
            var open = ListShown ? " combobox--open" : string.Empty;
            var extra = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? string.Empty : " " + CssClass;
            return $"combobox{open}{extra}";
        }
    }

    private string InputClass => Compact
        ? "field__input field__input--compact combobox__input"
        : "field__input combobox__input";

    private string OptionClass(int index) => index == _activeIndex
        ? "combobox__option combobox__option--active"
        : "combobox__option";

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (Value != _hostValue)
        {
            _hostValue = Value;
            var figure = Value ?? string.Empty;

            // An echo of the text already in the field is not a new figure.
            if (!string.Equals(figure, _text, StringComparison.Ordinal))
            {
                _text = figure;
                _committed = figure;
                _standing = figure;
            }
        }

        if (_activeIndex >= Options.Count) _activeIndex = -1;
    }

    private Task SetTextAsync(string? value)
    {
        _text = value ?? string.Empty;
        // A typed figure is not the option that was highlighted: Enter now commits
        // the text, not a suggestion the reader has typed past.
        _activeIndex = -1;
        return ValueChanged.InvokeAsync(_text);
    }

    private void Open()
    {
        if (!Disabled) _open = true;
    }

    /// <summary>A click in the field: the list opens on the option matching the
    /// field, as Down does, so the figure already there is the one highlighted and
    /// the next Down walks on from it. Nothing is highlighted when nothing
    /// matches, and a click on an open list moves nothing.</summary>
    private void OpenOnCurrent()
    {
        if (Disabled || ListShown) return;

        Open();
        _activeIndex = CurrentIndex();
    }

    private void Close()
    {
        _open = false;
        _activeIndex = -1;
    }

    /// <summary>The option whose value is in the field, where a list opened by the
    /// keyboard starts, or -1.</summary>
    private int CurrentIndex()
    {
        for (var i = 0; i < Options.Count; i++)
        {
            if (string.Equals(Options[i].Value, _text.Trim(), StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) return i;
        }

        return -1;
    }

    private async Task OnKeyDownAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (Disabled) return;

        var count = Options.Count;
        switch (e.Key)
        {
            case "ArrowDown":
                if (!ListShown)
                {
                    Open();
                    // Alt+Down shows the list and leaves the cursor in the text.
                    _activeIndex = e.AltKey || count == 0 ? -1 : Math.Max(CurrentIndex(), 0);
                }
                else if (count > 0)
                {
                    _activeIndex = (_activeIndex + 1) % count;
                }
                break;

            case "ArrowUp":
                if (!ListShown)
                {
                    Open();
                    var current = CurrentIndex();
                    _activeIndex = e.AltKey || count == 0 ? -1 : current >= 0 ? current : count - 1;
                }
                else if (count > 0)
                {
                    _activeIndex = (_activeIndex <= 0 ? count : _activeIndex) - 1;
                }
                break;

            case "Enter":
                if (ListShown && _activeIndex >= 0 && _activeIndex < count)
                {
                    await PickAsync(Options[_activeIndex]);
                }
                else
                {
                    Close();
                    await CommitAsync(ComboboxCommitReason.Entered);
                }
                break;

            case "Escape":
                if (ListShown)
                {
                    Close();
                }
                else if (_text.Length > 0)
                {
                    _text = string.Empty;
                    await ValueChanged.InvokeAsync(_text);
                }
                break;

            case "Tab":
                Close();
                break;
        }
    }

    private async Task PickAsync(SelectorOption option)
    {
        if (Disabled) return;

        _text = option.Value;
        Close();
        await ValueChanged.InvokeAsync(_text);
        await CommitAsync(ComboboxCommitReason.Picked);
    }

    private async Task OnChangeAsync(ChangeEventArgs args)
    {
        var text = args.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty;
        if (!string.Equals(text, _text, StringComparison.Ordinal))
        {
            _text = text;
            await ValueChanged.InvokeAsync(_text);
        }

        // The change a browser raises after Enter, or after a pick it saw as an edit,
        // carries the value already committed.
        if (string.Equals(text, _committed, StringComparison.Ordinal)) return;

        await CommitAsync(ComboboxCommitReason.Changed);
    }

    private async Task CommitAsync(ComboboxCommitReason reason)
    {
        _committed = _text;
        var commit = new ComboboxCommit(_text, reason);
        await OnCommit.InvokeAsync(commit);

        if (!commit.Refused)
        {
            _standing = commit.Value;
            return;
        }

        _text = _standing;
        _committed = _standing;
        // A host bound two-way holds the refused text as its Value; tell it the field
        // went back, or its next render would hand the refused text in again.
        if (!string.Equals(Value ?? string.Empty, _standing, StringComparison.Ordinal))
        {
            await ValueChanged.InvokeAsync(_standing);
        }
    }

    private string? Part(string name) => TestId is null ? null : $"{TestId}-{name}";
}
